te to a\nrequest that presented no valid token. For operating systems whose boot\nchain actually carries the token (Anaconda kickstart, CoreOS/Ignition),\nIP/MAC matching alone is not a sufficient boundary.\n\nIntroduce a static per-OS predicate Operatingsystem#token_enforced?\n(false by default, true for Redhat, Coreos, Fcos and Rhcos) rather than a\nDB column, since token support is a fixed property of the OS type. When an\nin-build host''s OS enforces the token, HostVerifier now requires a valid\ntoken (constant-time compared) and rejects tokenless IP/MAC-matched\nrequests; all other OSes keep the historical IP/MAC behavior.\n\nEnforcement is skipped in authenticated preview/spoof mode, is inert when\ntokens are disabled globally (token_duration = 0), and applies only to\nhosts in build mode.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n(cherry picked from commit ba630c13028fa18fac80ae0ef0590b15ef816dbf)","tree":{"sha":"56c0fb05ccdbd5e9e4408161fa8b6857380fff88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theforeman/foreman/git/trees/56c0fb05ccdbd5e9e4408161fa8b6857380fff88"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theforeman/foreman/git/commits/83c105d427bdfba941cdd9c4bd71da4d9cf7b2f9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/293363?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehelms/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehelms/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehelms/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehelms/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ehelms","id":293363,"login":"ehelms","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MzM2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehelms/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehelms/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehelms/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehelms/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehelms/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehelms","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theforeman/foreman/commit/83c105d427bdfba941cdd9c4bd71da4d9cf7b2f9","node_id":"C_kwDOAAPyvtoAKDgzYzEwNWQ0MjdiZGZiYTk0MWNkZDljNGJkNzFkYTRkOWNmN2IyZjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theforeman/foreman/commit/ce8bf3c05afa5f2919de348de5d6fddb9008bc6f","sha":"ce8bf3c05afa5f2919de348de5d6fddb9008bc6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theforeman/foreman/commits/ce8bf3c05afa5f2919de348de5d6fddb9008bc6f"}],"sha":"83c105d427bdfba941cdd9c4bd71da4d9cf7b2f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theforeman/foreman/commits/83c105d427bdfba941cdd9c4bd71da4d9cf7b2f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4253501?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pablomh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pablomh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pablomh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pablomh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pablomh","id":4253501,"login":"pablomh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNTM1MDE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pablomh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pablomh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pablomh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pablomh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pablomh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pablomh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theforeman/foreman/commits/ce8bf3c05afa5f2919de348de5d6fddb9008bc6f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-04T10:50:09Z","email":"pablomh@redhat.com","name":"Pablo Méndez Hernández"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T07:08:52Z","email":"github@stejskalleos.cz","name":"Leos Stejskal"},"message":"Fixes #39249 - Recover from false registration failures caused by TCP reset\n\nAt 320+ concurrent host registrations, the server sometimes creates the\nCandlepin consumer record successfully but the TCP connection is reset\nbefore the response reaches subscription-manager. This causes\n`subscription-manager register` to exit non-zero even though the\nregistration succeeded server-side, so the provisioning script fails a\nhost that is actually already registered.\n\nSince `register_katello_host` needs the consumer UUID regardless of\noutcome (it''s a required Foreman API param), the fix reframes the\nquestion from \"did register exit 0?\" to \"does a consumer UUID exist?\":\n\n- On success (`register` exits 0): reuse the UUID subscription-manager\n  already printed to its own stdout (\"The system has been registered\n  with ID: ...\"). No extra `subscription-manager identity` call is\n  spawned on this path. This isn''t just an assumption: `register` and\n  `identity` derive from the exact same Candlepin response object in\n  subscription-manager''s own source (`consumer[\"idCert\"]` is used both\n  to persist the cert and to print the ID), so the two are guaranteed\n  identical after a successful register - there is no correctness\n  trade-off in trusting the printed value.\n\n- On failure (`register` exits non-zero): fall back to\n  `subscription-manager identity`, which reads the local consumer cert\n  with no extra Candlepin round trip. If a UUID is found, the consumer\n  was created server-side and the response was simply lost in flight -\n  continue. If not, this is a genuine failure - exit as before (or\n  continue if `ignore_subman_errors` is set).\n\nThis keeps `subscription-manager identity` (measured at ~660ms/call,\nalmost entirely Python interpreter start-up, vs ~2ms for parsing text\nalready in memory) off the hot path: at 320+ concurrent registrations\nwhere the vast majority succeed on the first attempt, this removes one\nredundant subscription-manager invocation per host instead of adding\none. The rare recovery/failure paths are unchanged from the original\nproposal: exactly one identity call, used to distinguish a false\nnegative from a genuine failure.\n\nNo new script output is introduced (no REGISTRATION_SUCCESS /\nREGISTRATION_FAILED lines) - only subscription-manager''s own register\noutput is echoed back, matching the template''s existing behavior.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"4c8e911483518c2cf174e96ca46af03d127f7d9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theforeman/foreman/git/trees/4c8e911483518c2cf174e96ca46af03d127f7d9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theforeman/foreman/git/commits/ce8bf3c05afa5f2919de348de5d6fddb9008bc6f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59385976?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stejskalleos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stejskalleos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stejskalleos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stejskalleos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stejskalleos","id":59385976,"login":"stejskalleos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5Mzg1OTc2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stejskalleos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stejskalleos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stejskalleos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stejskalleos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stejskalleos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stejskalleos","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.