38892?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ericsaupe","id":5138892,"login":"ericsaupe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzg4OTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/instructure/canvas-lms/commits/3ff1fa4f4312eb8ebe3a1dfb2cc80776cfc382e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T18:20:58Z","email":"eric.saupe@instructure.com","name":"Eric Saupe"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T21:46:21Z","email":"eric.saupe@instructure.com","name":"Eric Saupe"},"message":"Fix todo list crash when points_possible is null\n\nAssignments can have null points_possible, causing the\ni18n pluralization call to return an object instead of\na string, crashing the entire to-do list.\n\nfixes LX-3610\nflag=none\n\ntest plan:\n- as a teacher with assignments that have no points\n  set, open the homeroom to-do list\n- verify the to-do list renders without crashing\n- verify assignments without points show no points label\n\nChange-Id: I5edc3a5e9dfdc7612962d799f26c04043a133bf8\nReviewed-on: https://gerrit.instructure.com/c/canvas-lms/+/407534\nTested-by: Service Cloud Jenkins <svc.cloudjenkins@instructure.com>\nQA-Review: June Eoh <jungsun.eoh@instructure.com>\nReviewed-by: June Eoh <jungsun.eoh@instructure.com>\nProduct-Review: Eric Saupe <eric.saupe@instructure.com>","tree":{"sha":"770bd28f985b162a8f26dae24a94996e595c26cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/instructure/canvas-lms/git/trees/770bd28f985b162a8f26dae24a94996e595c26cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/instructure/canvas-lms/git/commits/3ff1fa4f4312eb8ebe3a1dfb2cc80776cfc382e2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5138892?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ericsaupe","id":5138892,"login":"ericsaupe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzg4OTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericsaupe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/instructure/canvas-lms/commit/3ff1fa4f4312eb8ebe3a1dfb2cc80776cfc382e2","node_id":"C_kwDOABQOD9oAKDNmZjFmYTRmNDMxMmViOGViZTNhMWRmYjJjYzgwNzc2Y2ZjMzgyZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/instructure/canvas-lms/commit/d42433ba62388b5135a2687d1e2d407151d58005","sha":"d42433ba62388b5135a2687d1e2d407151d58005","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/instructure/canvas-lms/commits/d42433ba62388b5135a2687d1e2d407151d58005"}],"sha":"3ff1fa4f4312eb8ebe3a1dfb2cc80776cfc382e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/instructure/canvas-lms/commits/3ff1fa4f4312eb8ebe3a1dfb2cc80776cfc382e2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2695753?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanoto89/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanoto89/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanoto89/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanoto89/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chanoto89","id":2695753,"login":"chanoto89","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2OTU3NTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanoto89/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanoto89/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanoto89/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanoto89/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanoto89/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chanoto89","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/instructure/canvas-lms/commits/d42433ba62388b5135a2687d1e2d407151d58005/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-24T12:57:28Z","email":"christopher.soto@instructure.com","name":"Chris Soto"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T20:34:27Z","email":"christopher.soto@instructure.com","name":"Chris Soto"},"message":"add pagination to grading_rubrics api endpoint\n\nthis commit adds pagination and search for the grading_rubrics api\nendpoint under the certain situations:\n  - optimized_grading_rubrics is turned ON\n  - grading_rubrics_pagination is turned ON\n  - both FF are ON and paging params passed to api\n  - searches only when all above are true and there is a search term\nthis commit also introduces front end paging for the rubrics search\ntray that\n\ncloses EVAL-6820\nflag=optimized_grading_rubrics\nflag=grading_rubrics_pagination\n\ntest plan:\n- the paging on the front end is defaulted to 100. if you have less\n  rubrics than that, try changing the value\n  RUBRIC_FOR_CONTEXT_PAGINATION_LIMIT in file\n  ui/shared/rubrics/react/RubricAssignment/queries/index.tsx to a\n  smaller value.\n- with both FF ON, go to the assignments show page for an assignment\n- verify when opening the rubrics search tray, the pagination works as\n  expected when fetching rubrics for a course or account\n- verify that you can navigate to next page\n- try searching for rubrics and verify that:\n  - search results return correctly and paginated\n  - in the network tab, searching makes a backend request\n    (delayed 300ms)\n- verify after paging that if you switch to another context (course or\n  account), that the current page resets back to 1\n- verify that you can preview a rubric and attach it to an assignment\n- change the RUBRIC_FOR_CONTEXT_PAGINATION_LIMIT value to a number\n  greater than your current rubrics count\n- verify that the results are no longer paginated and also when\n  searching, that we don''t make any network requets. all searches under\n  the default paging size should stay on front end only\n\nthe remaining steps will validate that the feature works as is when\n  the needed FFs are disabled\n- reset the RUBRIC_FOR_CONTEXT_PAGINATION_LIMIT to a smaller value and\n  turn off the optimized_grading_rubrics FF.\n- verify that pagination is not happening\n- turn back on optimized_grading_rubrics but turn off the\n  grading_rubrics_pagination FF and verify that the results are not\n  paginated\n\nChange-Id: I2c1e42da5ebe68748392a9dff728df3d98b2d91a\nReviewed-on: https://gerrit.instructure.com/c/canvas-lms/+/407302\nTested-by: Service Cloud Jenkins <svc.cloudjenkins@instructure.com>\nReviewed-by: Derek Williams <derek.williams@instructure.com>\nReviewed-by: Rajmund Csehil <rajmund.csehil@instructure.com>\nQA-Review: Derek Williams <derek.williams@instructure.com>\nProduct-Review: Yasi Afsharnive <yasaman.afsharnive@instructure.com>","tree":{"sha":"9fc4fe78e9e2d1c627480c1dde5047a86e79c142","url":"https://api.github.com